# CODEOWNERS - auto-request review for every PR.
#
# GitHub assigns these owners as required reviewers on any PR that touches a
# matching path.  This file lives at the repo root (GitHub also accepts
# .github/CODEOWNERS or docs/CODEOWNERS).
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Only the LAST matching pattern applies, so the catch-all comes first and
# each block below narrows it.  There is one maintainer today, so every block
# names the same owner.  They are listed separately anyway: the file then
# records which areas are treated as review-sensitive, and adding a second
# owner for an area becomes a one-line edit rather than a re-derivation of
# this list.

# Catch-all: the repository root and anything not matched below.
*                       @brandontroidl

# Subsystems.
/docs/                  @brandontroidl
/modules/               @brandontroidl
/weather_providers/     @brandontroidl
/tests/                 @brandontroidl

# CI and repository automation.  A change here alters what runs on every PR.
/.github/               @brandontroidl
/.github/workflows/     @brandontroidl

# Security-sensitive: credential storage, password hashing, and the
# tamper-evident audit trail.
/secret_store.py        @brandontroidl
/hashpw.py              @brandontroidl
/audit_log.py           @brandontroidl
